WEBVTT

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:05.400
Here is an oldie, but a goodie
for finishing the edges of your knitting.

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:09.520
It's not only pretty,
it can also help tame the curl of plain

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:15.040
stockinette knitting. Once you understand
it and get a feeling for how it's worked,

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:20.240
there are lots of variations
to this trim that you can employ.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:27.240
Working from right to left with the purl
side of your knitting facing,

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:32.160
use a three prong tool and hang the edge
of the knitting on three needles.

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:34.320
Set your carriage for plain knitting

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:37.560
at a tension slightly tighter
than your garment tension.

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:40.080
Knit four to six rows.

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:44.320
You'll want to experiment
with the tension for yourself.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:49.880
Moving along to the left,
pick up the edge again with the three

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:55.880
prong tool and hang the edge
on those same three needles.

00:00:55.960 --> 00:01:00.120
Knit the same number of rows.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:03.920
Keep picking up the edge stitches and hang

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:09.160
them on those same three needles
and knit the same number of rows.

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:12.520
Continue in this manner
until you reach a corner.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:15.880
At the corner, knit an extra two rows

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:21.080
and then continue picking
up the edge of the knitting.

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:31.840
In this example, we knit four rows between
pickups and the texture isn't as defined.

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:34.400
Experiment with your yarn.

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:38.760
You can also fluff up the trim
by picking up in this stitch,

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:40.400
again.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:45.120
Pick up the edge,
hang it on three needles,

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:50.560
knit four to six rows, pick up the edge,
hang it on the same needles,

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:54.280
knit four to six rows,
and continue all the way around the edge

00:01:54.360 --> 00:02:02.360
of your garment
and you'll have a beautiful, worm trim.

